BT /F1 12 Tf 50 750 Td 16 TL (OFFICIAL STATISTICAL SYSTEM: SURVEY METHODOLOGY AND FIELD MANUAL) ' () ' (1. Introduction to Survey Design and Frame Construction) ' () ' (A sampling frame is an exhaustive list of all eligible sampling units in the target population.) ' () ' (Stratified random sampling is used when the population naturally divides into non-overlapping homogeneous strata.) ' () ' (Stratification reduces overall sampling variance and guarantees proportional representation of minority domains.) ' () ' (2. Computer Assisted Personal Interviewing \(CAPI\) Protocols) ' () ' (CAPI enables field enumerators to capture respondent data directly on mobile tablets without persistent network connectivity.) ' () ' (Offline synchronization stores encrypted records locally and transmits them to central servers once connectivity is restored.) ' () ' (Validation rules built into CAPI prevent illegal range entries and contradictory cross-field responses in real time.) ' () ' (3. Non-Sampling Error Minimization and Quality Control) ' () ' (Non-sampling errors arise from factors such as respondent misreporting, enumerator bias, and data entry mistakes.) ' () ' (Supervisory spot-checks and re-interviews are mandatory quality control procedures to detect systematic interviewer errors.) ' () ' (Imputation techniques and sampling weight adjustments are used to correct for unit and item non-response.) ' ET
endstream
